From 98401b0ca81c3095ab63be17f66e8e3136b74029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:55:51 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Preview FastLED Patterns through the shared render loop
 (local #9002)

A FastLED previewSource takes its own branch in the Preview build effect:
@pxlblz-dim drives the default layout, defines = {PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS (map
pixel count), PXLBLZ_WIDTH/HEIGHT for regular grids}; the compiled module
comes from fastledStore (compiled on demand when missing, with a
"Compiling FastLED Pattern..." overlay, or a friendly German notice when
the compile service is offline: the launcher starts it, otherwise
`npm run service` in fastled-integration). The host is instantiated
asynchronously (cancel-guarded), seeded per Pattern, persisted Control
values are applied before the first frame, and the FastLED handle runs
through startLoop: same renderer, paintPacked and external pixel output,
so the router receives FastLED's exact wire bytes. Always the fast shim.

- LED-count mismatch and runaway-budget notices use the renderAdaptation
  readout.
- Control values of FastLED Patterns persist per Pattern (debounced
  updatePatternControls, keyed by FastLED UI name, only real changes).
- ControlsPanel/readout: ranged sliders show raw values with the FastLED
  min/max/step; Pixelblaze sliders unchanged.

Pre-commit hook checks run manually (hook cannot spawn npx.cmd on Windows/Node 24):
npm run lint, check:e2e-coverage, check:e2e-locators, tsc -b (tsconfig + node),
vitest Preview + ControlsPanel + previewPanel + renderLoop + src/engine/fastled (75 passed).

